{"trace_id": "9163c2b8a3b44fef", "events": [{"event_type": "model.invoke", "trace_id": "9163c2b8a3b44fef", "span_id": "e32f0446b08e4d00", "parent_span_id": "b194ce19dd144513", "span_name": null, "sequence_id": 1, "timestamp_ns": 1784076924371288000, "payload": {"name": "ollama.chat", "model": "llama3:8b", "latency_ms": 4576.406955718994, "parameters": {"model": "llama3:8b"}, "messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are an on-premise clinical decision-support assistant running entirely inside the hospital network \u2014 no patient data leaves the building. You support licensed clinicians and are not a substitute for clinical judgement. Answer concisely (under 150 words)."}, {"role": "user", "content": "A 68-year-old outpatient is diagnosed with community-acquired pneumonia (CURB-65 score 1), has no drug allergies, normal renal and hepatic function, and has not been hospitalized or on antibiotics in the last 90 days. Suggest a reasonable first-line oral antibiotic regimen and the two most important things to monitor or counsel the patient on."}], "output_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "For this outpatient with community-acquired pneumonia, I recommend a first-line oral antibiotic regimen of azithromycin (500mg PO qd for 5-7 days) or doxycycline (100mg PO bid for 7-10 days).\n\nTwo important things to monitor or counsel the patient on:\n\n1. Monitor for signs of worsening infection, such as increased fever, chest pain, or shortness of breath. If these symptoms occur, consider adjusting therapy or hospitalizing the patient.\n2. Educate the patient on the importance of completing the full course of antibiotics and not sharing their medication with others to prevent antibiotic resistance."}, "otel_gen_ai": {"gen_ai.system": "ollama", "gen_ai.operation.name": "chat", "gen_ai.request.model": "llama3:8b", "gen_ai.response.model": "llama3:8b", "gen_ai.response.finish_reasons": ["stop"], "gen_ai.usage.input_tokens": 134, "gen_ai.usage.output_tokens": 130}, "